hadiths[10]{hadithnumber,text}:
"22844","Abdullah ibn Muhammad ibn Abi Shaybah narrated to us, and I heard it myself from Ibn Abi Shaybah in Kufa, and Ibn Abi Shaybah said to us in it from az-Zuhri, and as for my father, he narrated it to us from him without mentioning az-Zuhri, and he narrated it to us in Kufa, making it for us from az-Zuhri, then he returned to the hadith of my father. Jafar ibn Awn narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Ismail: Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah informed me, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, sent him alone as a scout to Quraysh. He said: So I came to the wood of Khubayb while fearing watchers, and I climbed it and untied Khubayb, and he fell to the ground. So I withdrew not far, then I looked and did not see Khubayb, as though the earth had swallowed him, and no trace of Khubayb was seen until this hour."
"22845","Abu Amir narrated to us: Ali narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah: Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah informed me, from his father, that he saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiping over the two khuffs."
"22846","Abu Amir narrated to us: Fulayh narrated to us, from az-Zuhri: Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah narrated to me, from his father, that he saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, eat a limb in the prayer place and not perform ablution."
"22847","Abu Abdur-Rahman narrated to us: Haywah narrated to us: Ayyash ibn Abbas informed us that Kulayb ibn Subh narrated to him that az-Zibriqan narrated to him, from his uncle Amr ibn Umayyah ad-Damri, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on one of his journeys, and he slept past the dawn prayer until the sun rose; they did not wake. And indeed the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, began with the two rakahs and prayed them, then the prayer was established and he prayed."
"22848","Abu al-Mughirah narrated to us: Abdur-Rahman ibn Amr al-Awzai narrated to us: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir al-Yamani narrated to me, from Abu Salamah, from Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah ad-Damri, from his father, that he saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wipe over the two khuffs and the turban."
"22849","Muhammad ibn Musab narrated to us: al-Awzai narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, from Abu Salamah, from Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah ad-Damri, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiping over the two khuffs and the khimar."
"22850","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq: Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah narrated to me, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiping over the two khuffs."
"22851","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Salih: Ibn Shihab said: Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah narrated to me that his father said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, cutting from a shoulder of sheep, then he was called to prayer, so he threw the knife and did not perform ablution."
"22852","Yaqub narrated to us: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Shihab, from Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah, from his father, who said: I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, eating, cutting from a shoulder, then he was called to prayer, so he prayed and did not perform ablution."
"22853","Hasan ibn Musa and Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, both saying: Shayban narrated to us, from Yahya, from Abu Salamah, that Jafar ibn Amr ibn Umayyah ad-Damri informed him that his father informed him that he saw the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, wiping over the two khuffs."
